r 130 hours.\n\nWhen i saw the dlc i bought it, but found all my save data gone with no way to restore it.\nBig ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ F and the only game i ever had this problem with. \n\nJust disapointed to lose all those hours of playtime with no chance to get it back. \n\nAnd no its not normal in this day and age. especially with cloud saves to have to make a local back up for a game. They ♥♥♥♥♥♥ up and it costs me 130 h..", "timestamp_created": 1701373645, "timestamp_updated": 1701373645, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "152599734", "author": {"steamid": "76561198003225239", "personaname": "-Deicide-", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198003225239/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 15, "playtime_forever": 3699, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1633, "last_played": 1714592772, "avatar": "6ee2b77f5c79d32797c2910524431b93bdd3837c"}, "language": "english", "review": "Game is good my only real complaint is no cross progression saves. I bought it to play with my buds and nothing you do in their game saves to your own. Weapons, levels yes, but map exploration and key progression check points = no. I absolutely hate running  one shot puzzles 50+ times ... So with that being said, not really a game for me.", "timestamp_created": 1701372239, "timestamp_updated": 1701372314, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "152599421", "author": {"steamid": "76561198053744623", "personaname": "Sam-pie", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/sam724/", "num_games_owned": 1173, "num_reviews": 123, "playtime_forever": 6435, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1262, "last_played": 1754148473, "avatar": "f786ba6a6a8928eb867bdb5422f80c7f89959dee"}, "language": "english", "review": "Some good ideas badly stitched together, like some kind of Frankenstein's Monster. I did not enjoy this game and don't care enough about it to go into detail, would not reccomend.", "timestamp_created": 1701371872, "timestamp_updated": 1701371872, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "152599280", "author": {"steamid": "76561197984790565", "personaname": "semeku", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/smeegu/", "num_games_owned": 1497, "num_reviews": 89, "playtime_forever": 7462, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5088, "last_played": 1757770191, "avatar": "3491bd38b0a0cb5953185c56ac5b5d8dbd727a38"}, "language": "english", "review": "26.04.2024\nWith the release of the new DLC the game is still an utter mess when it comes to optimization. It's impossible for me to enjoy this game. It's a stuttery mess. Game refuses to fully even use my GPU. \nI can make the game look like a fried potato, but the fps is STILL absolutely terrible and the frametimes are all over the place. No matter what settings I use.\n\n[h1]DO NOT BUY THIS GAME IF YOU DON'T HAVE JUST THE RIGHT GPU & CPU COMBO THAT MAGICALLY MAKES THE GAME RUN GOOD.[/h1]\n\nTo start, the game is great, but the reason why I'm NOT recommending is the abysmal or simply lazy optimization done with this game. I've only played solo so I have no experience how multiplayer will affect performance, but I can only guess it's not gonna be any better....\n\nThe base game runs \"OK\", but it also isn't a smooth experience. You can look at the fps numbers all day long, but when the frametimes jump from 20ms to 60ms (during combat) the ride is not smooth no matter how high the fps number is.\n\nWith the first DLC the new area is an abysmally horrible experience. The fps and frametimes are all over the place.\n\nI've yet to find any setting combination that truly makes the game feel smooth. Native vs DLSS performance or ultra performance makes very little difference here. The graphic settings from ULTRA to POTATO also doesn't impact as much as it should. Changing resolution to 1080 or 1440p also has very little impact on how smooth the game feels.\n\nThis makes me think the rendering in this game is fundamentally broken here and needs a lot of work to get fixed.\n\nFor comparison Cyberpunk 2077 with RT Overdrive on feels more smooth than Remnant 2. Let that sink in.\n\n1440p \ni7-10700k\n32 GB RAM\nRTX3080TI\nInstalled on Samsung 980 PRO NVME SSD", "timestamp_created": 1701371712, "timestamp_updated": 1714146309, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "152599057", "author": {"steamid": "76561197971470401", "personaname": "Milan", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Korovyov/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 18881, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 15259, "last_played": 1733196554, "avatar": "e1dde7fe207a397634580d4755f7890ccf24ddd7"}, "language": "english", "review": "awesome gameplay, great co-op support, broad build variety, buy it now!", "timestamp_created": 1701371489, "timestamp_updated": 1701371489, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.52173912525177002", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "152598647", "author": {"steamid": "76561197976439306", "personaname": "Ryven", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/CasualHeroes/", "num_games_owned": 837, "num_reviews": 14, "playtime_forever": 53066, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 65, "playtime_at_review": 30178, "deck_playtime_at_review": 3, "last_played": 1788553216, "avatar": "c3a815c510b7c6b16b893f807efe70bf839e37ef"}, "language": "english", "review": "Remnant 2 is my GOTY. It truly hits everything that I want in an ARPG and SoulsLike game. When Remnant: From The Ashes came out, I felt like it released out of no where and it was a solid game. Gun Fire games blew all my expectations out of the water with Remnant 2. 10/10 for me this year. Lets cover why. \n\nArchetypes:\nI love the archetype system and the freedom to mix and match and try crazy class combinations, mixed with the myriad of items to choose from there are truly endless options for builds, the 500 hours I have put in a is a mix of just exploring every nook and cranny and trying different archetypes and truly learning the pros and cons between them. This is such a fun and robust system even between DLCs it keeps me coming back.\n\nItems:\nThe items that you are rewarded feel purposeful and useful. While some are stronger, build into a meta and just down right OP. There is a ring, weapon, amulet or relic that fits into some type of play style. Again the builds are endless. I am still farming to complete all 100% of the base and DLC items and I cannot wait for more. \n\nCombat:\nIf you played RFtA then you know the combat. Tho Rem2 feels much cleaner, more responsive and over all just high adrenaline rush while in combat. The combat is fun and engaging keeping you on your toes especially in higher difficulties. The boss fights are a blast, i enjoyed them very much. My biggest complaint in combat is the Apocalypse modifiers on bosses. These can stop your build dead, and then you either just push through it or find away to adapt it. Probably my biggest pet peeve with modifiers and I would love to see them add an option to turn them off when re-rolling adventures/campaigns. Otherwise combat is amazing. \n\nWorld:\nThe worlds this time around are amazing. Probably my favorite and among the many others is Losmon, the Bloodborne English Elvin setting just feels amazing. Root Earth, while a royal pain in my arse, I love the design and feel of it. Yaesha was just a typical jungle and Ner'ud my least favorite in terms of enemies but my favorite in terms of aesthetics. Only Gun Fire Games found away to make all these unique worlds work together. They are blast to explore (except Ner'ud, cause vomiting is always fun) and the randomization does add some fresh play to the worlds on each new role. \n\n\nWeapons/Mods/Mutators/Skills:\nThis is where the game shines, the Weapons/Mods/Mutators/Skills are unique, thought out and just fun. Turning into a lightning overload that can teleport while dishing out constant lighting building up crit dmg while your turret has infinite ammo and a fire tornado is spinning around killing all the enemies it pulls in, never felt so good. GunFireGames did an outstanding here and while some guns do lack punch or fit into a build, they are all fun to just play around with and see what works where. \n\n\nPerformance:\nThis is where the game has issues, and its really tough on PC. I run a 7950x with a 7900xt and 32GB of and Samsung SSDs across the board and I could be consistently at 120FPS then just walking i drop to 15 FPS for no reason. I have played with so many settings, I actually ended up turning off AMD Smart Access Memory and this help stabilize the fluctuation of my FPS and instead of dropping down to 15 from 120, i drop to 60. There is for sure much work that needs to be done here, as I do not encounter this in any other game.  Hopefully the devs can figure it out and optimize the game. \n\n\nDLC:\nThe DLC for me was a blast. All though short, I beat it in about 5 hours, the lore of Lomson has been fabulous. The fights are awesome and I am still discovering secrets as I go. I 100% recommend the DLC, even tho i feel the release of it hindered the performance of the game even more.\n\nOverall:\nRemnant 2 has struck some many cords over the other glaring issues it has, performance, some design choices and other little annoying factors like buggy items (Brewmasters Cork) otherwise this game is a 10/10 for me and shows that if a company actually cares and has good leadership and not chasing the games wallet amazing games can be made. I look forward to the future of Remnant and the DLCs and  hopefully some neat game modes. \n\nWish List:\n-Performance fixes\n-Survivor mode (rogue like)\n-Boss Rush mode Timed with leader boards/Untimed\n-Relics slots for armor\n-Option to turn off modifiers\n-Harder difficulty\n-higher respawn rate on apparition \n-API to easily develop databases for character builders / calculators\n\nThanks for reading! See you in game!", "timestamp_created": 1701371042, "timestamp_updated": 1701371174, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.525862038135528564", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "152596102", "author": {"steamid": "76561198025565020", "personaname": "SaPMESS", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198025565020/", "num_games_owned": 162, "num_reviews": 13, "playtime_forever": 1159, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1137, "last_played": 1701368249, "avatar": "aa9f0d354713edfffd38aa326b10c83a91d9d784"}, "language": "english", "review": "Loved it! Just finished the game (on veteran difficulty). This is the first game in a while (other than maybe Elden Ring) where I've found myself loving the atmosphere and just saying \"whoa\" when fighting a boss etc.\n\nEvery boss fight felt like a good amount of progress for me, understanding move sets etc., and while the last boss can be chaotic, I felt like it was the right step up in terms of difficulty - definitely felt like a last boss\n\nI'm not sure if the adventure mode currently has enough for me to keep playing but this was one of my favourite games (of 2023 but also of all time), loved it.", "timestamp_created": 1701368148, "timestamp_updated": 1701368148, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "152595703", "author": {"steamid": "76561198217396555", "personaname": "SUBEME LA RADIO", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/martnsson/", "num_games_owned": 132, "num_reviews": 22, "playtime_forever": 3251, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 3008, "last_played": 1740397943, "avatar": "5d2541364dbdc0bc1b2d8311b2d2c02780b5252b"}, "language": "english", "review": "Remnant 2 is a video game.", "timestamp_created": 1701367722, "timestamp_updated": 1701987998, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.466507166624069214", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "16